# Fujitsu ScanSnap iX500 (Evernote Edition, 04c5:13f3).
# Give the device a stable systemd unit name (dev-scansnap.device) and start the
# user's scan-button service whenever it's plugged in / switched on.
# Must match every action except remove: USB devices get "add" then "bind",
# and a rule that skips "bind" loses the systemd tag (service starts, then stops).
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", \
  ATTR{idVendor}=="04c5", ATTR{idProduct}=="13f3", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_ALIAS}+="/dev/scansnap", \
  ENV{SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS}+="scan-button.service"
